exports[`gate commands > /waive by rule writes one reason under each item of the rule, by line under one item; the checklist moves on and the record names the rule 1`] = `
{
  "afterAll": [
    "- [x] 4. Errors fixed or waived: none open in findings.md",
    "- [ ] 6. Export to Word: ready",
    "Next step for you: step 6.",
  ],
  "afterRule": [
    "- [ ] 4. Fix or waive the Errors: 1 open (findings.md line 11)",
    "Next step for you: step 4.",
  ],
  "byLine": "Waived 1 Error(s) in drafting/hinge/findings.md (line 11) with the reason under each item; recorded in drafting/hinge/draft-application.working-record.md.",
  "byRule": "Waived 2 Error(s) in drafting/hinge/findings.md (lines 7, 8) with the reason under each item; recorded in drafting/hinge/draft-application.working-record.md.",
  "definedTermLine": 11,
  "findings": "# Findings

Errors and Inventor Questions block export until they are resolved or waived. To waive one, add a line \`  - Waived: <reason>\` under it. Notes never block. Advisory items come from the model review; they are advice, not a pass.

## Errors

- \`antecedent-basis\` (claims.md, line 4, claim 2): Claim 2: "the clamp body" has no antecedent basis.
  - Waived: False positive: "a clamp body" is in claim 1.
- \`antecedent-basis\` (claims.md, line 5, claim 3): Claim 3: "the pin" has no antecedent basis.
  - Waived: False positive: "a clamp body" is in claim 1.
- \`defined-term\` (draft-application.md, line 12): Line 12 writes "clamp-body"; the defined term is "clamp body".
  - Waived: Client spelling.

## Inventor Questions

None.

## Notes

None.

## Advisory

None.
",
  "record": [
    "- **Error waived:** antecedent-basis (2 item(s), findings.md lines 7, 8) by the attorney in chat (command /waive) at <time>",
    "- **Error waived:** defined-term (1 item(s), findings.md line 11) by the attorney in chat (command /waive) at <time>",
  ],
}
`;
